    "details": "Starman project reports:\n\n> \\[SECURITY\\]\n>\n> - Stream chunked request bodies to the temporary buffer instead of\n>   holding whole chunks in memory (CVE-2026-115824)\n> - Parse chunk-size lines in linear time with a 4 KiB length limit and\n>   strict syntax; malformed lines get 400 (CVE-2026-115822)\n> - Do not send a response body for HEAD requests or 1xx, 204 and 304\n>   responses, on both the array and streaming paths (CVE-2026-115823)\n> - Limit how long a request body may take to arrive: \\--read-timeout\n>   (default 5 seconds) now also applies to each wait for more of the\n>   body, and the new \\--body-timeout option limits the total time\n>   (default 300 seconds; raise it or set it to 0 for slower uploads).\n>   Expiry gets 408 (CVE-2026-115817)\n> - Reject Transfer-Encoding other than \\\"chunked\\\" (400/501) and close\n>   the connection after a request with both Transfer-Encoding and\n>   Content-Length. Completes the fix for CVE-2026-40560\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0560",
